            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Many examinations have limitations, including specificity. Therefore, multiple examinations should be combined for practical diagnosis to facilitate treatment. In symposium 14 (ultrasound and clinical examina- tion), 5 speakers presented how to combine diagnostic methods in their clinical practice. This symposium highlighted the importance of the comprehensive management of multiple examinations for optimal patient care.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
